{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"Getting Started with Gnusto"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"By the end of this guide you will have a game with two rooms, one object, one rule, and a test that plays it. It assumes you can write basic Swift; it assumes nothing about interactive fiction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Prefer to start from something that already runs? ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bin\/new-game Zwank ~\/dev\/Zwank"},{"text":" writes a complete starter package named for your game — then skim this guide for the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"why"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" behind each piece.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Add-Gnusto-to-your-package","type":"heading","text":"Add Gnusto to your package","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Gnusto as a dependency, list it in your executable target, and give the test target the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GnustoTestSupport"},{"type":"text","text":" product (it links the toolchain’s Testing library, so it belongs in test targets only):"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ swift-tools-version: 6.2","import PackageDescription","","let package = Package(","    name: \"MyGame\",","    platforms: [.macOS(.v15)],","    dependencies: [","        .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/HeirloomLogic\/Gnusto\", from: \"0.1.0\")","    ],","    targets: [","        .executableTarget(","            name: \"MyGame\",","            dependencies: [","                .product(name: \"Gnusto\", package: \"Gnusto\")","            ]","        ),","        .testTarget(","            name: \"MyGameTests\",","            dependencies: [","                \"MyGame\",","                .product(name: \"GnustoTestSupport\", package: \"Gnusto\"),","            ]","        ),","    ]",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gnusto needs a Swift 6.2 toolchain and the Swift 6 language mode. The "},{"code":".macOS(.v15)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" floor above is "},{"code":"Synchronization.Mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; Linux is tested in CI and needs no platform line. iOS is supported too, at "},{"code":".iOS(.v18)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for the same reason. Add that line if your game is an app rather than a terminal program, and give it an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler"},{"type":"text","text":" of its own — see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Declare-a-game","level":2,"text":"Declare a game"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A game is a single type conforming to ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game"},{"text":". Start with just a title and an intro:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","","struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" requires an ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", but Swift synthesizes it for free as long as every stored property has a default value — which they always will here, since rooms, items, and state are declared with initializers."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Add-a-room","level":2,"text":"Add a room"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" as a stored property. The property name ("},{"code":"hall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") becomes the room’s internal identity; the ","type":"text"},{"code":"name(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" trait is what the player sees.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct MyGame: Game {","    let title = \"My First Game\"","    let intro = \"A cool breeze drifts down the hall.\"","","    let hall = Location {","        name(\"Entrance Hall\")","        description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","    }","","    var map: WorldMap {","        player.starts(in: hall)","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block is where geography and starting positions live. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"player.starts(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" places the player; without it, the game has nowhere to begin."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Run it","anchor":"Run-it","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two lines turn a game value into a running session:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()"]},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","type":"reference"},{"text":" validates the game and builds its initial state up front — a mistake like an exit to an undeclared room is caught here, as a thrown ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError","type":"reference"},{"text":", not at runtime. ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","type":"reference"},{"text":" runs the prompt\/parse\/perform\/print loop, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler","type":"reference"},{"text":" reads from and writes to the terminal.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Wrap it in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"do"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"catch"},{"type":"text","text":" in your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"main.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Gnusto","","do {","    let world = try GameWorld(game: MyGame())","    await REPL(world: world, io: ConsoleIOHandler()).run()","} catch {","    print(\"Couldn't start the game: \\(error)\")","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Run "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swift run"},{"type":"text","text":", and you can already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"look"},{"type":"text","text":" around and try to move."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Add-a-second-room-and-connect-them","text":"Add a second room and connect them","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exits are declared on locations in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"map"},{"type":"text","text":" block. Each directional method ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", …) is an ordinary property reference, so a typo or a renamed room is a compile error, not a broken game.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let hall = Location {","    name(\"Entrance Hall\")","    description(\"A long hall of grey stone. A doorway opens to the north.\")","}","","let library = Location {","    name(\"Dusty Library\")","    description(\"Shelves sag under mildewed books. The hall lies south.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Exits are one-directional by design — declare both ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hall.north(library)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"library.south(hall)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" if you want the player to be able to walk back."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Add-a-thing","type":"heading","text":"Add a thing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Declare an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","type":"reference"},{"text":" the same way, then place it in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"map","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let lantern = Item {","    name(\"brass lantern\")","    adjectives(\"brass\", \"old\")","    description(\"An old brass lantern, its glass sooty but intact.\")","}","","var map: WorldMap {","    hall.north(library)","    library.south(hall)","","    player.starts(in: hall)","    lantern.starts(in: library)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the player can walk "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"north"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"examine lantern"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"take lantern"},{"text":", and see it in their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inventory"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" let them type ","type":"text"},{"code":"take brass lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"take old lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a phrase has to end on a noun, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"take brass","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on its own is not one of them. The last word of ","type":"text"},{"code":"name(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (“lantern”) is the noun the parser keys on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything you declare is split into words the same way the parser splits what the player types — lowercased, a trailing possessive dropped, every other punctuation mark a separator. So "},{"code":"name(\"Mrs. Vane\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" prints its period and answers to "},{"code":"mrs vane","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"adjectives(\"master's\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same declaration as "},{"code":"adjectives(\"master\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Write the second: a declaration should read the way the parser stores it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"React-with-a-rule","level":2,"text":"React with a rule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So far every verb uses its built-in behavior. To add your own logic, write a rule in the "},{"code":"rules","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block. Rules are "},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" hooks attached to a location, an item, or the whole world."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var rules: Rules {","    lantern.after(.take) {","        say(\"It's heavier than it looks.\")","    }","","    library.before(.go) {","        guard command.direction != .south else { return }","        try refuse(\"There's no exit that way — only back south to the hall.\")","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first rule runs "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the player successfully takes the lantern and adds a line of flavor with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The second runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" movement in the library and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"s any direction but south. Inside a rule body, bare identifiers like "},{"code":"command","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"player","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and your own "},{"code":"lantern","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" refer to the live turn — reading and writing them touches the current game state.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To learn what rules can do — the phases, the ordering, and the difference between "},{"code":"refuse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"reply","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"say","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" — read ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Test it","type":"heading","anchor":"Test-it"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A play session is just typed input and printed output, so the natural test plays a scripted session and asserts on the transcript:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","struct MyGameTests {","    @Test func theLanternIsWhereTheBreezeSaysItIs() async throws {","        let transcript = try await play(MyGame(), [\"north\", \"take lantern\"])","        expectInOrder(transcript, [\"Dusty Library\", \"Taken.\"])","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"play"},{"type":"text","text":" boots the game and feeds it each command; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectInOrder"},{"type":"text","text":" asserts the beats appear in order and shows the full transcript when one doesn’t. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for turn slicing and pinning the random stream."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"A fuller example","level":2,"anchor":"A-fuller-example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Gnusto ships with "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Cloak of Darkness","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", Roger Firth’s classic one-room demonstration game, as its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CloakOfDarkness"},{"type":"text","text":" target. It exercises nearly every feature in a page of code — dark rooms, a wearable cloak, scored actions, a losing state, and per-turn rules — and is worth reading start to finish once the basics click."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Next steps","level":2,"anchor":"Next-steps"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bin\/new-game"},{"text":" in the repo — writes the complete starter package this guide builds up to","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","isActive":true},{"text":" — how declarations, identity, and live references fit together","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"},{"type":"text","text":" — exactly what happens each turn"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — the full vocabulary of game logic"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — teach the parser new words with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#verb"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — transcript tests with GnustoTestSupport"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — carry your own data on entities and in globals"}]}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GettingStarted","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Build and run your first text adventure, one piece at a time.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/gettingstarted"]}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","abstract":[{"text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world.","type":"text"}],"title":"Writing Rules","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Item":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A thing in the world."}],"title":"Item","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Item","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Item"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/item","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AddingCustomVerbs":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/addingcustomverbs","abstract":[{"text":"Teach the parser words the built-in table doesn’t know.","type":"text"}],"title":"Adding Custom Verbs","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/south(_:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An exit leading south to ","type":"text"},{"code":"to","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"south(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/south(_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/south(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"south"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV","text":"Location","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV","text":"MapEntry","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/REPL":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/REPL","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"REPL"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"REPL"}],"title":"REPL","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/repl","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The outer loop: prompt → parse → perform → print, until the game ends or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"input runs out. Holds the only "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a Gnusto game."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/say(_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"say","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/say(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Prints a message as part of the turn’s output."}],"title":"say(_:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/say(_:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Game":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Game"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/game","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A complete game: declarations, geography, and rules."}],"title":"Game","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Game","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location/north(_:)":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"north(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location\/north(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"An exit leading north to ","type":"text"},{"code":"to","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location\/north(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"north"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Location","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8LocationV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8MapEntryV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MapEntry"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline","abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"title":"The Turn Pipeline","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/IOHandler":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IOHandler"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IOHandler"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/iohandler","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IOHandler","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where the game’s text goes and player input comes from. Synchronous by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"design: a blocking console read is fine for a CLI; an async variant can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be added later without breaking this protocol’s clients."}],"title":"IOHandler","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TestingYourGame":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/testingyourgame","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TestingYourGame","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Play scripted sessions in your test suite and assert on the transcript."}],"title":"Testing Your Game","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/CustomFrontEnds":{"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Custom Front Ends","abstract":[{"text":"Putting the engine behind something that is not a terminal.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/customfrontends","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomFrontEnds"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/adjectives(_:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Additional words the parser accepts before the item’s noun."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"adjectives(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/adjectives(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"adjectives"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"...) -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto9ItemTraitV","text":"ItemTrait"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"type":"topic","title":"Gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/refuse(_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refuse"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","text":"Never"}],"title":"refuse(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/refuse(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Blocks the current action with a complaint. The default action and any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remaining ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rules are skipped; world time still passes.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AnatomyOfAGame":{"type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AnatomyOfAGame","title":"Anatomy of a Game","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/anatomyofagame","abstract":[{"text":"How a single Swift type becomes a world the engine can run.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/ConsoleIOHandler":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConsoleIOHandler"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ConsoleIOHandler"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/consoleiohandler","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Plain terminal IO.","type":"text"}],"title":"ConsoleIOHandler","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/ConsoleIOHandler","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/BootstrapError":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BootstrapError","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BootstrapError","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"BootstrapError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"All problems with a game definition, reported at once."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/bootstraperror","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapError"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameWorld":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameWorld","fragments":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GameWorld","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"GameWorld","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gameworld","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The game world: owns all state, serializes all mutation, and runs the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turn pipeline. The single "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":" in a game sits between the REPL and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this actor."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/CustomStateAndTraits":{"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Carry your own data on entities and in globals, alongside the engine’s closed core.","type":"text"}],"title":"Custom State and Traits","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/customstateandtraits","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/CustomStateAndTraits"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Location":{"type":"topic","title":"Location","abstract":[{"text":"A place in the world.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Location","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/location","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Location"}]}}}